model {
  extend basalt.build {
    metadata {
      constraint "E2E scenarios that install Playwright's controlled browser clock through the shared helper see whole-millisecond Date.now() values, as a real browser reports. The controlled clock keeps fractional timer delays, such as a jittered reconnect, so its Date.now() can land between milliseconds; Effect converts Date.now() to BigInt for span timing, so such a value fails a request before it is sent and a fenced read accepts the stale result. The account outage polling proof starts its controlled clock half a millisecond off a whole value so this condition is exercised on every run. Product polling, fencing and request code are unchanged."
    }
  }
}
